{"trace_id":"heliotrope_bluehearth_2024_q17","title":"Nexora Thermal Systems, Inc. / BlueHearth Logistics Controls, Ltd. — approval risk note","body":"The acceptance gate is express: the HSR waiting period, including any extension, must have expired or terminated. This is the defined Regulatory Condition in Annex II; it is not merely a general representation about legal compliance. [nexora_bluehearth_2024__03_merger_agreement__d0147]

The parties must submit the HSR filing promptly and no later than the fifteenth business day after signing, request early termination under the agreed process, and not withdraw except in connection with agreement termination. Other required antitrust filings must also be made promptly. The cooperation provisions include sharing specified substantive agency communications and giving the other side’s outside counsel an opportunity to review and comment on planned written communications. [nexora_bluehearth_2024__03_merger_agreement__d0091]

The remedy obligation is sharply limited. Section 7.2(d) does not require Nexora to divest or hold separate facilities or equipment lines, license technology, alter contractual relationships, change operations, or accept restrictions on ownership and operation. BlueHearth cannot discuss or commit to the listed remedies without Parent’s prior written consent in its sole discretion. The practical risk allocation therefore combines a clearance condition and procedural cooperation with substantial buyer control over substantive concessions. [nexora_bluehearth_2024__03_merger_agreement__d0094]","artifact_directory":"artifacts"}

{"trace_id":"aureline_morrowspan_2025_t07","title":"Aureline / MorrowSpan — approval risk note","body":"The two votes use different tests. At the Scheme Meeting, approval requires a majority in number representing at least 80% in value of members or the relevant class present and voting, personally or by proxy. At the general meeting, the shareholder resolution requires at least 80% of the voting rights of eligible members present and voting. The contractual definition therefore preserves a headcount element for the scheme vote that does not appear in the general-meeting test. [aureline_morrowspan_2025__03_agreement__c0217]

Article VIII also requires the shareholder approvals, court sanction, absence of a continuing prohibitory order or illegality, and expiration, termination or receipt of the applicable national-security, subsidy-control and foreign-investment clearances or waiting periods. These are common closing conditions for the transaction. [aureline_morrowspan_2025__03_agreement__c0141]

Sanction and effectiveness are separate steps. On the closing date MorrowSpan must deliver the sanctioning order to the Registrar of Companies in England and Wales; that delivery makes the scheme effective. It must also give Aureline the order and reasonable evidence of effectiveness, making delivery evidence a distinct checklist item. [aureline_morrowspan_2025__03_agreement__c0009]","artifact_directory":"artifacts"}

{"trace_id":"asterion_bluehaven_2027_t09","title":"Asterion Robotics Ltd. / BlueHaven Water Systems plc — approval risk note","body":"The agreement conditions closing on expiration or termination of the HSR and specified competition waiting periods, receipt of other identified competition, investment-screening and infrastructure approvals, and the absence of blocking restraints. Those approval conditions must be satisfied without a Burdensome Condition, and the restraint condition also covers measures that impose or purport to impose one. [asterion_bluehaven_2027__02_agreement__d0176]

Both sides undertake reasonable best efforts regarding filings, information requests and timely clearance. Asterion makes the final determination as to required or advisable filings and, after good-faith consultation and consideration of BlueHaven’s views, directs regulatory communications, negotiations, timing, strategy and related litigation. The consultation obligation therefore remains applicable even though Asterion controls the strategy. [asterion_bluehaven_2027__02_agreement__d0154] [asterion_bluehaven_2027__02_agreement__d0155]

The remedies covenant covers transfers or licenses of BlueHaven equipment platforms, software, contracts and operating units, other business limitations, and pursuit of challenges. But Asterion need not take action reasonably expected to materially impair BlueHaven as a whole, materially reduce the expected value of the combination, or have more than an incidental effect on a material Asterion business line or product family. Those are the defined Burdensome Condition limits. The drafting establishes a substantial but bounded efforts obligation, not an unlimited commitment to accept every regulatory concession. [asterion_bluehaven_2027__02_agreement__d0156]","artifact_directory":"artifacts"}

{"trace_id":"lattice_bluequartz_2027_t09","title":"Lattice Harbor Infrastructure Fund, through Lattice Harbor Water Holdings LLC / Bluequartz Water Systems, Ltd. — approval risk note","body":"Bluequartz’s required approval is adoption by holders of at least fifty-eight percent of the outstanding voting units entitled to vote. The agreement identifies this as the only class or series approval needed for the transaction; it is also a condition to all parties’ closing obligations. This is an outstanding-units threshold, so a simple majority of units actually voted is not the stated test. [lattice_bluequartz_2027__03_merger_agreement__c0034] [lattice_bluequartz_2027__03_merger_agreement__c0096]

The buyer separately benefits from Section 7.4(c): governmental consents, clearances, permits, notices and other specified actions must occur, and applicable waiting periods must end, as identified in the disclosure-schedule provision. The review note should track that contractual category without naming agencies not supplied by the clause. The shared no-impediment condition separately covers specified laws, orders and governmental proceedings that prohibit or materially impair the transaction or payment. [lattice_bluequartz_2027__03_merger_agreement__c0097] [lattice_bluequartz_2027__03_merger_agreement__c0096]

On the acquisition-vehicle side, Parent must approve the agreement as Merger Sub’s sole member and manager promptly after execution, no later than five business days afterward, and deliver evidence to Bluequartz. That is an affirmative authorization covenant to track alongside the closing conditions. [lattice_bluequartz_2027__03_merger_agreement__c0093]","artifact_directory":"artifacts"}

{"trace_id":"syn","title":"Borealis Tidal Systems plc, through Borealis Tidal Holdings Ltd. / LumenHarbor Robotics Oy — approval risk note","body":"The defined Regulatory Approvals expressly include Canadian National Security Clearance, Norwegian Marine Infrastructure Clearance, Singapore Port Technology Clearance and Brazilian Competition Approval, together with other necessary or advisable approvals identified in the referenced disclosure schedule. Section 8.2(e) conditions completion on those approvals or expiration or termination of relevant waiting periods, unless waived by Parent in its sole discretion. The agreement also requires that no effective Restraining Order prohibit the Transactions. [borealis_lumenharbor_2028__02_agreement__c0028] [borealis_lumenharbor_2028__02_agreement__c0116]

Shareholder action remains a separate gate: adoption of the Asset Transfer Resolutions, Combination Resolutions and Board Composition Resolutions at the special meeting or a later meeting is an express offer condition. Receipt of the Final Norwegian Tax Confirmation is separately specified. [borealis_lumenharbor_2028__02_agreement__c0116]

The parties must coordinate filings and strategy, cooperate and use reasonable best efforts to obtain clearances promptly; Parent bears filing fees. That efforts covenant has substantial boundaries. Parent, Purchaser and their Affiliates are not obligated to divest businesses, vessels, technology or other assets, alter specified relationships or rights, accept restrictions on retained operations, or litigate or contest regulatory proceedings and orders. A clearance-risk assessment must preserve those express limitations. [borealis_lumenharbor_2028__02_agreement__c0091] [borealis_lumenharbor_2028__02_agreement__c0092]","artifact_directory":"artifacts"}

{"trace_id":"syn","title":"Nereid Harbor Technologies, Inc., through Nereid Harbor Acquisition LLC / Quaystone Marine Robotics, Inc. — approval risk note","body":"The stockholder condition requires the Requisite Stockholder Approval at the stockholder meeting. Section 3.4 defines that approval as the affirmative vote of holders representing more than one-half of the voting power of all outstanding common shares entitled to vote, voting together as one class, subject to its stated assumption regarding Nereid Harbor’s and Merger Sub’s Section 4.8 representations. It is not a majority merely of votes cast. [nereid_quaystone_2027__06_agreement__c0048] [nereid_quaystone_2027__06_agreement__c0116]

The HSR condition requires expiration or termination of applicable waiting periods, extensions or review periods, or receipt of each required consent. The agreement separately requires CFIUS Approval and the absence of a prohibitive restraint. A form communication from the FTC Bureau of Competition substantially resembling the specified February 2024 template does not, by itself, cause the no-restraint condition to fail. [nereid_quaystone_2027__06_agreement__c0116] [nereid_quaystone_2027__06_agreement__c0117]

Following the contemplated joint voluntary notice, CFIUS Approval can consist of written clearance confirming that review is complete and no unresolved national-security concern remains, referral followed by presidential nonintervention, including no action during the 15-day period, or written confirmation that the transaction is not covered. Counsel should therefore collect evidence for the applicable defined route. [nereid_quaystone_2027__06_agreement__c0009]","artifact_directory":"artifacts"}
